# Production safety

This repo deploys straight to production. There is no staging. These limits are not optional.

## What production looks like

| Thing | Value |
|-------|-------|
| Public site | `https://www.amixof.com` (client at `/`, `/login`; API at `/api/`) |
| Compose file | `/opt/stoat/compose.yml` (project dir `/opt/stoat`) |
| Service you may touch | `web` (container `stoat-web-1`) — **only this one** |
| Image naming | `amixof-for-web:<7-char commit sha>`, built on the server |
| Build dirs | `/root/amixof-builds/amixof-for-web-<sha>` |
| Backups | `/root/amixof-backups/<UTC yyyymmdd-HHMMSS>/compose.yml` + `previous-image` |
| SSH target | `AMIXOF_SSH` in `.cursor/amixof.env` (never commit that file) |
| Source repo | `https://github.com/karbuunofficial/amixof-for-web` (`amixof` remote, `main`) |

The `web` container serves static files on port 5000 and replaces `__VITE_*__` placeholders at
startup (`docker/inject.js`). Runtime URLs come from the compose environment, not the build.

## Always

- Deploy only with `.cursor/skills/amixof-deploy/scripts/deploy.sh`. It refuses dirty or unpushed
  trees, takes a lock so two deploys cannot overlap, backs up the compose file, swaps only `web`,
  checks the live site, and rolls back by itself if the checks fail.
- Roll back only with `.cursor/skills/amixof-rollback/scripts/rollback.sh <last|backup|tag>`.
- See what is live with `.cursor/skills/amixof-rollback/scripts/status.sh` (read-only).
- Other read-only inspection over SSH is fine: `docker ps`, `docker compose ps`,
  `docker logs --tail 200 stoat-web-1`, `df -h`, `grep -n 'image:' /opt/stoat/compose.yml`.
  Do not `cat` the compose file or any `.env`: they hold credentials.
- After any production change, run the `amixof-prod-check` skill.

## Never

- Never run `docker compose down`, `docker compose up` without `--no-deps <service>`,
  `docker compose restart` without a service name, `docker system prune`, `docker volume rm/prune`,
  `docker rm -f` on anything but a failed `web` container, or `rm -rf` on the server.
- Never edit `/opt/stoat/compose.yml` by hand, or change any line except the `amixof-for-web` image tag.
- Never touch the API, database (MongoDB), Redis/KeyDB, RabbitMQ, MinIO/S3, mail, LiveKit, or
  reverse-proxy containers or their config. If a task seems to need that, stop and ask the user.
- Never read, print, copy, or commit secrets: `.env` files on the server, `Revolt.toml`, SSH keys,
  tokens, user data. Do not paste server env vars into chat or commits.
- Never run database queries or migrations against production.
- Never deploy from a branch other than `main`, a dirty tree, or a commit that is not on GitHub.
  AGPL requires the running code to be published; the server builds from GitHub for that reason.
- Never force-push `main`. Never rewrite published history.
- Never delete backups or old images to free space without asking the user first.

## If something goes wrong

1. If the site is broken by a deploy you made: run `rollback.sh last` immediately, then confirm
   with `amixof-prod-check`. If deploy.sh exited 4, the server already restored the previous
   image; do not roll back again.
2. Collect `docker logs --tail 200 stoat-web-1` and the deploy log in `.cursor/artifacts/`.
3. Report what happened, what you rolled back to, and what you still need from the user.
